verif:Obl_token_replay_counts_corr a verif:CorrespondenceObligation ;
  verif:corrOrder 1 ;
  verif:corrName "token_replay_counts_corr" ;
  verif:rustSymbol "wasm4pm_core::conformance_counts" ;
  verif:rustFile "wasm4pm-core/src/conformance_counts.rs" ;
  verif:leanDecl "ProcInt.ReplayCounts" ;
  verif:aeneasModule "Wasm4pmVerify.Generated" ;
  verif:aeneasDecl "ReplayCounts" ;
  # verif:status is NOT asserted here — it is a builder-derived field, owned
  # exclusively by scripts/build_verif.py, which emits it into the sibling
  # generated fragment fragments/verif-status.generated.ttl (same subject
  # IRI, this predicate only) from observed evidence. Defaults to "DECLARED"
  # when no charon/aeneas/lake evidence exists yet. Never hand-set here.
  verif:obligationStatement """theorem token_replay_counts_corr
    (gen : Wasm4pmVerify.Generated.ReplayCounts)
    (hm : gen.missing.val ≤ gen.consumed.val)
    (hr : gen.remaining.val ≤ gen.produced.val) :
    let spec := Wasm4pmVerify.toSpec gen hm hr
    (spec.missing_le = hm) ∧
    (spec.remaining_le = hr) ∧
    (ProcInt.fitness spec =
       (1 - (gen.missing.val : ℚ) / (gen.consumed.val : ℚ)) / 2 +
         (1 - (gen.remaining.val : ℚ) / (gen.produced.val : ℚ)) / 2) ∧
    (fitness_num gen = Result.ok (core.num.U64.saturating_sub gen.consumed gen.missing)) ∧
    ((fitness_den gen = Result.ok Option.none ∨ ∃ d, fitness_den gen = Result.ok (Option.some d))) := by
  intro spec
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rfl
  · rfl
  · rfl
  · rfl
  · unfold fitness_den
    cases h : U64.checked_add gen.produced gen.remaining with
    | none => left; rfl
    | some d => right; exact ⟨d, rfl⟩""" ;
  verif:note "Pilot correspondence obligation (D1 of the plan's Part D ordering). rustFile is wasm4pm-core/src/conformance_counts.rs (already split out of the wasm4pm-compat façade per Part A), which holds the ReplayCounts{produced,consumed,missing,remaining} struct and fitness_num/fitness_den integer functions; leanDecl joins procint:Decl_ReplayCounts (packs/lean-math-pack/fragments/conformance.ttl, module Conformance.TokenReplay). Status is builder-derived by scripts/build_verif.py from observed charon/aeneas/lake evidence, never hand-set here. Conjunct 1 (ProcInt.fitness unfolds to the Rozinat-Aalst formula) is definitional (rfl). Conjunct 2 substitutes hnum_src/hden_src, then discharges the ℕ-truncated-subtraction-vs-ℤ-subtraction gap via Nat.cast_sub, using the ReplayCounts proof field missing_le : missing ≤ consumed (the ℕ addition side needs no such lemma — addition never truncates)." .
